<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ambystoma mexicanum Schnakenberg onset wavelength at 184.3 µm (Pass 2) — Code-to-model traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Docstring, dispersion function, and Lean module MathOfBiology.Loop_3107 still name the same Jacobian integers, the eight-wavelength patch, and the positive onset numerator. Pass 2 comments separate the homogeneous onset law from the shallow source gradient. Lean was not executed in this environment (no lean binary); the proofs are decide/integer and contain no sorry." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ambystoma mexicanum Schnakenberg onset wavelength at 184.3 µm (Pass 2) — Model fidelity to source: 89/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The homogeneous law is unchanged and checked: trace −0.2, det 1, ratio 9 above r_c ≈ 8.568, onset wavenumber fixed at 2π/184.3 µm, linear fastest mode 187.19 µm. Pass 2 integrates from noise. The shell that wins is n = 8, the onset shell, rather than a mode that was planted in the initial condition. A shallow source gradient of amplitude 0.12 is an extra term, stated as such. The dispersion cusp is the discriminant branch point (vertical tangent where disc = 0), drawn on a 900-point grid and labeled." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ambystoma-mexicanum-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ambystoma mexicanum Schnakenberg onset wavelength at 184.3 µm (Pass 2) — Morphometric validation: 87/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Continuum versus periodic-shell Pearson r = 0.999595, RMSE = 2.02 µm, residual CV = 0.0089. The reference for r is 1, and the measured value is not 1. Linear fastest wavelength 187.19 µm versus onset 184.3 µm. Noise-selected shell 184.3 µm (n = 8). Band-weighted wavelength 176.47 µm, which is not the reference. Specimen dark fraction 0.380 versus model 0.314. Specimen coherency 0.485 versus model 0.904. Luminance KS = 0.302. Radial-spectrum r = 0.910. No specimen number is copied onto its reference, and the photo is not given a false micrometre scale." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
